From: joethedev5 <deepsbx1@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:27:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 41/45] Complete the PRR integration in the duplicate-ACK and
 output paths

The reference calls tcp_prr_update from the already-in-fast-recovery
duplicate-ACK branch before the legacy SACK/awnd or plain cwnd update,
and accounts every transmitted segment in tp->prr.out at the end of
tcp_output.  The partial-ACK call was already in place.

Authored-By: joethedev5 <joeshmo@nunya.com>
---
 bsd/netinet/tcp_input.c  | 4 +++-
 bsd/netinet/tcp_output.c | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bsd/netinet/tcp_input.c b/bsd/netinet/tcp_input.c
index af007e959..0c297fc8f 100644
--- a/bsd/netinet/tcp_input.c
+++ b/bsd/netinet/tcp_input.c
@@ -3862,7 +3862,9 @@ process_dupack:
 					 * to keep a constant cwnd packets in the
 					 * network.
 					 */
-					if (SACK_ENABLED(tp) && IN_FASTRECOVERY(tp)) {
+					if (tcp_prr && IN_FASTRECOVERY(tp)) {
+						tcp_prr_update(tp, th);
+					} else if (SACK_ENABLED(tp) && IN_FASTRECOVERY(tp)) {
 						int awnd;
 
 						/*
diff --git a/bsd/netinet/tcp_output.c b/bsd/netinet/tcp_output.c
index c9d21fcf2..ad6bf3f9c 100644
--- a/bsd/netinet/tcp_output.c
+++ b/bsd/netinet/tcp_output.c
@@ -3139,6 +3139,10 @@ out:
 
 	tcpstat.tcps_sndtotal++;
 
+	if (tcp_prr && IN_FASTRECOVERY(tp)) {
+		tp->prr.out += len;
+	}
+
 	KERNEL_DEBUG(DBG_FNC_TCP_OUTPUT | DBG_FUNC_END, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0);
 	if (sendalot) {
 		goto again;
